    "ENG_4": {
      "code": "ENG",
      "category_name": "Data Engineering",
      "status": "BLOCKED",
      "prerequisites": [
        "ENG_1",
        "ENG_2",
        "ENG_3",
        "ACQ_3"
      ],
      "details": "Overall, the 14 publications reported on 62 unique study sites (38 burned), spanning wildfires occurring between 1947 and 2016, and contributed a total of 52 effect sizes to the meta-analysis."
    },
    "DEV_1": {
      "code": "DEV",
      "category_name": "Model Development",
      "status": "BLOCKED",
      "prerequisites": [
        "ENG_4"
      ],
      "details": "We quantify changes in DOC concentrations after wildfires, by the natural log of the response ratio (lnRR) (Hedges et al., 1999): lnRR = ln(Y1/Y2) (1); vlnRR = s1^2/(n1 Y1^2) + s2^2/(n2 Y2^2) (2); RR = exp(lnRR) (3), where Y1 and Y2 are the mean DOC concentrations, n1 and n2 are the sample sizes, and s1 and s2 are the standard deviations for the treatment and control, respectively. We back-transformed lnRR estimates using the exponential function to obtain the Response Ratio (RR) (Equation (3)), and reported the values in percentages to facilitate interpretation."
    },
