      "details": "We addressed non-independence by employing hierarchical (multilevel) models to accommodate the non-independence effect. Additionally, to represent repeated measures through time, we accounted for a model with a heteroscedastic autoregressive (HAR) structure (Viechtbauer, 2010). This approach allows variances to differ across time periods when non-independence occurs."
    },
    "DEV_3": {
