{"project":"Replicating-MBRS-Iowa-River-2023","workflow":{
  "DSGN_1":{
    "code":"DSGN",
    "category_name":"Methodological Design",
    "status":"READY",
    "prerequisites":[],
    "details":"Reproducible pilot study to estimate Iowa River discharge using MBRS framework with PCA-ESTARFM over ice-free season (2023-04-01 to 2023-11-30). Steps: (1) Acquire Landsat 8/9 L2 and Sentinel-2 L2A imagery (<20% cloud) over 15×15 km box around USGS gauge 05454500; acquire USGS daily mean discharge (cfs→m³/s). (2) Generate river mask by NDWI + 50 m buffer. (3) Identify same-day cloud-free base pairs; resample/reproject Landsat to 10 m grid. (4) Apply PCA to base pairs, select similar pairs, then run ESTARFM for synthetic 10 m time series. (5) Compute eight optical indicators per pixel inside mask; align with discharge dates. (6) Compute pixel-wise Pearson correlations; select top 7 % RGPs; compute spatial mean; adjust sign; smooth via TRES. (7) Train Ridge (MBRS-RD) and Random Forest (MBRS-RF) with grid search & 10-fold CV; predict 2023 period; compute NSE, R², RMSE, MAE; plot hydrograph. (8) Monte Carlo uncertainty: vary RGP thresholds (4–10 %) over 100 runs; extract 5th/95th percentiles; plot uncertainty bounds."
  },
  "INFRA_1":{
    "code":"INFRA",
    "category_name":"Infrastructure",
    "status":"READY",
    "prerequisites":["DSGN_1"],
    "details":"On Windows 11, install Python packages via pip: rasterio, geopandas, numpy, pandas, scikit-learn, scikit-image, scipy, pystac-client, sentinelsat, landsatxplore, owslib, usgs-waterdata, matplotlib, seaborn. Do not use apt-get or sudo."
  },
  "ACQ_SAT":{
    "code":"ACQ",
    "category_name":"Data Acquisition",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["INFRA_1"],
    "details":"Write `01_acquire_satellite.py`. Define 15 km×15 km bounding box centered on lat/lon of USGS gauge 05454500. Use landsatxplore to search/download Landsat 8/9 Level-2 scenes and sentinelsat to search/download Sentinel-2 Level-2A scenes between 2023-04-01 and 2023-11-30 with cloud cover <20 %. Save raw images in `data/satellite/`.",
    "ui_instructions":{
      "type":"instruction",
      "prompt":"Set your Copernicus and USGS API credentials as environment variables before running the script."
    }
  },
  "ACQ_USGS":{
    "code":"ACQ",
    "category_name":"Data Acquisition",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["INFRA_1"],
    "details":"Write `02_acquire_usgs.py`. Query the USGS water services API for gauge 05454500 daily mean discharge (cfs) from 2023-04-01 to 2023-11-30. Convert cfs to m³/s (1 cfs = 0.0283168 m³/s). Save to `data/usgs_discharge_cms.csv`."
  },
  "ENG_CleanUSGS":{
    "code":"ENG",
    "category_name":"Data Engineering",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["ACQ_USGS"],
    "details":"Write `03_clean_usgs.py`. Load `data/usgs_discharge_cms.csv`, parse date column, fill any missing dates with NaN, forward-fill or interpolate missing discharge values, and save cleaned file `data/clean_usgs_discharge.csv`."
  },
  "ENG_RiverMask":{
    "code":"ENG",
    "category_name":"Data Engineering",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["ACQ_SAT"],
    "details":"Write `04_generate_river_mask.py`. Select the clearest high-flow Sentinel-2 image from `data/satellite/`. Calculate NDWI = (Green−NIR)/(Green+NIR). Threshold NDWI>0 to create water mask. Buffer mask outward by 50 m using geopandas. Save shapefile `masks/river_mask.shp`."
  },
  "INSP_RiverMask":{
    "code":"INSP",
    "category_name":"Manual Inspection",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["ENG_RiverMask"],
    "details":"Visualize `masks/river_mask.shp` over a base Sentinel-2 image to verify bank coverage and buffer. Confirm mask accurately delineates river corridor.",
    "ui_instructions":{
      "type":"human_review",
      "prompt":"Open `masks/river_mask.shp` in your GIS viewer. Does the buffer fully cover the river banks without including buildings? (yes/no)"
    },
    "cyclic_routing":{
      "condition":"User approval",
      "if_true":["ENG_ClipImages"],
      "if_false":["ENG_RiverMask"]
    }
  },
  "ENG_ClipImages":{
    "code":"ENG",
    "category_name":"Data Engineering",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["INSP_RiverMask","ACQ_SAT"],
    "details":"Write `05_clip_images.py`. Loop over all raw images in `data/satellite/`, clip each to `masks/river_mask.shp`, and save clipped rasters to `data/satellite_clipped/`."
  },
  "ENG_BasePairIdentification":{
    "code":"ENG",
    "category_name":"Data Engineering",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["ENG_ClipImages"],
    "details":"Write `06_identify_base_pairs.py`. Scan metadata of clipped Landsat and Sentinel images, identify dates with both scenes cloud-free on same day. Save list of base pairs with file paths to `metadata/base_pairs.csv`."
  },
  "INSP_BasePairs":{
    "code":"INSP",
    "category_name":"Manual Inspection",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["ENG_BasePairIdentification"],
    "details":"Review `metadata/base_pairs.csv` to ensure correct matching of dates and file integrity. Confirm that base pairs represent clear water scenes.",
    "ui_instructions":{
      "type":"human_review",
      "prompt":"Check the first 5 entries of `metadata/base_pairs.csv`. Are these correct base pairs? (yes/no)"
    },
    "cyclic_routing":{
      "condition":"User approval",
      "if_true":["ENG_ResampleReproject"],
      "if_false":["ENG_ClipImages"]
    }
  },
  "ENG_ResampleReproject":{
    "code":"ENG",
    "category_name":"Data Engineering",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["INSP_BasePairs"],
    "details":"Write `07_resample_reproject.py`. For each Landsat image in base pairs, resample to 10 m resolution and reproject to the CRS and grid alignment of Sentinel-2 using rasterio. Save outputs to `data/base_pairs_resampled/`."
  },
  "INSP_Alignment":{
    "code":"INSP",
    "category_name":"Manual Inspection",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["ENG_ResampleReproject"],
    "details":"Overlay a resampled Landsat and corresponding Sentinel-2 scene to check pixel alignment. Confirm perfect grid alignment and no drift.",
    "ui_instructions":{
      "type":"human_review",
      "prompt":"Visualize one base pair overlay in GIS or matplotlib. Is alignment satisfactory? (yes/no)"
    },
    "cyclic_routing":{
      "condition":"User approval",
      "if_true":["DEV_PCA"],
      "if_false":["ENG_ResampleReproject"]
    }
  },
  "DEV_PCA":{
    "code":"DEV",
    "category_name":"Model Development",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["INSP_Alignment"],
    "details":"Write `08_compute_pca.py`. Load resampled base-pair images for all spectral bands, stack as feature matrix, perform PCA across pixels. Save principal components arrays to `data/pca_components/`."
  },
  "DEV_SelectSimilar":{
    "code":"DEV",
    "category_name":"Model Development",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["DEV_PCA"],
    "details":"Write `09_select_similar_pairs.py`. For each target date without base pair, compute Euclidean distance in PCA space between target and each base pair. Select the most similar base-pair scenes for ESTARFM inputs. Save mapping to `metadata/similar_pairs.csv`."
  },
  "DEV_DefineESTARFM":{
    "code":"DEV",
    "category_name":"Model Development",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["DEV_SelectSimilar"],
    "details":"Write `10_define_estarfm.py`. Implement ESTARFM function taking Landsat and Sentinel inputs, spectral weights, window size, and PCA-based similarity mapping. Provide API to fuse two base dates to target date."
  },
  "EXEC_RunESTARFM":{
    "code":"EXEC",
    "category_name":"Execution",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["DEV_DefineESTARFM"],
    "details":"Write `11_run_estarfm.py`. For each target date in 2023-04-01–2023-11-30, call ESTARFM with selected similar base pairs. Generate synthetic 10 m multi-band images. Save to `data/fused/`."
  },
  "ENG_CalcIndicators":{
    "code":"ENG",
    "category_name":"Data Engineering",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["EXEC_RunESTARFM"],
    "details":"Write `12_calc_indicators.py`. For each fused image in `data/fused/`, clip to `masks/river_mask.shp` and compute eight indicators: NDWI, ANDWI, TWI, Red, BSI, NDVI, NDMI, NIR per pixel. Store outputs per date as NetCDF or CSV in `data/indicators/`."
  },
  "ENG_AlignTimeseries":{
    "code":"ENG",
    "category_name":"Data Engineering",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["ENG_CalcIndicators","ENG_CleanUSGS"],
    "details":"Write `13_align_timeseries.py`. Load indicator files and `data/clean_usgs_discharge.csv`. Align by date: merge on date, drop mismatches, output unified DataFrame `data/timeseries_aligned.csv`."
  },
  "INSP_TimeseriesAlignment":{
    "code":"INSP",
    "category_name":"Manual Inspection",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["ENG_AlignTimeseries"],
    "details":"Plot sample indicator time series against discharge for a few pixels. Verify correct date alignment and value ranges.",
    "ui_instructions":{
      "type":"human_review",
      "prompt":"Review time series plot. Is alignment correct? (yes/no)"
    },
    "cyclic_routing":{
      "condition":"User approval",
      "if_true":["DEV_Corr"],
      "if_false":["ENG_AlignTimeseries"]
    }
  },
  "DEV_Corr":{
    "code":"DEV",
    "category_name":"Model Development",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["INSP_TimeseriesAlignment"],
    "details":"Write `14_compute_correlations.py`. Load `data/timeseries_aligned.csv`, compute Pearson correlation per pixel for each of the eight indicators vs. daily discharge. Save correlations to `analysis/pixel_correlations.csv`."
  },
  "ENG_SelectRGP":{
    "code":"ENG",
    "category_name":"Data Engineering",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["DEV_Corr"],
    "details":"Write `15_select_rgps.py`. For each indicator, select top 7% of pixels by absolute correlation. Compute the spatial mean of these Remote Sensing Gauging Pixels per date. Multiply indicator values by -1 where correlation is negative. Save `analysis/rgp_timeseries.csv`."
  },
  "DEV_TRES":{
    "code":"DEV",
    "category_name":"Model Development",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["ENG_SelectRGP"],
    "details":"Write `16_define_tres.py`. Implement Time-sensitive Recursive Exponential Smoothing filter with parameter α=0.3 (or configurable). Provide function to smooth RGP time series."
  },
  "EXEC_ApplyTRES":{
    "code":"EXEC",
    "category_name":"Execution",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["DEV_TRES"],
    "details":"Write `17_apply_tres.py`. Load `analysis/rgp_timeseries.csv`, apply TRES filter to each indicator time series, output smoothed series to `analysis/rgp_timeseries_smoothed.csv`."
  },
  "DEV_TrainModels":{
    "code":"DEV",
    "category_name":"Model Development",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["EXEC_ApplyTRES"],
    "details":"Write `18_train_models.py`. Load smoothed features and discharge. Define Ridge Regression (MBRS-RD) and RandomForestRegressor (MBRS-RF). Set up grid search over α for Ridge and n_estimators/max_depth for RF. Configure 10-fold CV. Save best models as `models/ridge.pkl` and `models/rf.pkl`."
  },
  "EXEC_Predict":{
    "code":"EXEC",
    "category_name":"Execution",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["DEV_TrainModels"],
    "details":"Write `19_predict_discharge.py`. Load `models/ridge.pkl` and `models/rf.pkl`, apply to 2023 features. Save predictions to `analysis/predictions.csv`."
  },
  "EVAL_Performance":{
    "code":"EVAL",
    "category_name":"Evaluation",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["EXEC_Predict"],
    "details":"Write `20_evaluate_models.py`. Load predictions and actual discharge. Compute NSE, R², RMSE, MAE. Generate and save hydrograph plot comparing observed vs simulated flows as `outputs/hydrograph.png`. Save metrics in `outputs/performance_metrics.json`."
  },
  "DEV_DefineMonteCarlo":{
    "code":"DEV",
    "category_name":"Model Development",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["EXEC_Predict"],
    "details":"Write `21_define_monte_carlo.py`. Define Monte Carlo simulation varying RGP selection threshold randomly between 4% and 10% for each of eight indicators. Plan 100 simulation runs looping through `15_select_rgps.py`, TRES, model prediction steps."
  },
  "EXEC_MonteCarlo":{
    "code":"EXEC",
    "category_name":"Execution",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["DEV_DefineMonteCarlo"],
    "details":"Write `22_run_monte_carlo.py`. Execute 100 Monte Carlo runs: for each run, select RGPs with random thresholds, smooth with TRES, predict discharge using saved models. Aggregate all run predictions into `analysis/mc_predictions.csv`."
  },
  "EVAL_Uncertainty":{
    "code":"EVAL",
    "category_name":"Evaluation",
    "status":"BLOCKED",
    "prerequisites":["EXEC_MonteCarlo"],
    "details":"Write `23_uncertainty_analysis.py`. Load `analysis/mc_predictions.csv`, compute 5th and 95th percentiles per date. Plot uncertainty hydrograph ribbon over observed and simulated median flows. Save bounds to `outputs/uncertainty_bounds.json` and plot to `outputs/uncertainty_hydrograph.png`."
  }
}}

